Chapter: SpawnMemoTable

  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 What is guarded is that a spawned child inherits the memo-table base, not the
 character value: `from-unicode` is here only because it is the shortest call
 that materialises a memoized definition. The arm that can fail is QEMU. Under
 Renode a lost base reads address 0 without faulting, so the cache misses
 forever, the table is rebuilt on every call, and this test answers correctly
 whether the base arrived or not.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Concurrent, Console] Integer
  opening = act
    pid <- process-spawn (\x -> poke-byte 28000 0 (from-unicode 69))
    let y = process-yield
    in peek-byte 28000 0
  end
